- an alternative to littlenavmap-bin which is more lightweight(-400% less disk space usage as some small performance gains. You'll notice less stutters when zooming in or out the map when there are lots of items enabled)
- qt6 support with docking on wayland too
- attemps to use system libraries, likewise it respects system theme
- the xplane plugin (little xpconnect) is built too, against a static qt from littlenavmap-qt6-base-static so it only needs glibc. install it with Tools > Install Little Xpconnect (needs X-Plane set up and its database selected) or copy /usr/lib/littlenavmap/Little Navmap/Little Xpconnect into X-Plane/Resources/plugins
- littlenavmap-qt6-base-static is only a build dependency. building it takes a while, you can install the prebuilt package from https://github.com/Denzy7/littlenavmap-qt6-base-static_PKGBUILD/releases with `sudo pacman -U <file>` instead
- its bleeding edge so if you have any pkgbuild issues delete the src first
- the first build clones the full upstream repos (marble is large), later builds only fetch what changed
- only build issues should be reported here. use upstream to report application issues
- you can download the latest CI build at https://github.com/Denzy7/littlenavmap-git_PKGBUILD/actions (the artifacts are the .pkg.tar.zst files themselves, install with `sudo pacman -U <file>`)
